flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a Cloudflare Worker goes live
    accDescr: You merge a pull request into main, after every required check passed. Workers Builds of Cloudflare builds the commit with the lock file of the repository and runs npm run deploy, whose script asks whether the commit is a release. An ordinary commit becomes a version of the Worker without traffic, which the dashboard lists. The merge of the release pull request goes live with its version; the release workflow tags the same commit and publishes the release on GitHub, with its SBOMs and signed provenance. No key of Cloudflare is stored in GitHub.

    merge["You merge a pull request into main"]
    build["`*Workers Builds* of Cloudflare builds the commit with **package-lock.json**, with no key of Cloudflare in GitHub`"]
    ask["`**npm run deploy** asks: is the commit the release of **package.json**?`"]
    upload["`No: a version without traffic, listed with its commit`"]
    live["`Yes, *chore: release X.Y.Z*: it goes live as **vX.Y.Z**`"]
    release["`The release workflow tags the same commit and publishes the release, with SBOMs and provenance`"]

    merge --> build --> ask
    ask --> upload
    ask --> live
    merge --> release

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class merge you
    class build,ask,release bot
    class upload,live done
